and a subject a loop writer composes). Every commit of a loop lane must carry a present, well-formed trailer, a person's commit included, which otherwise belongs in the person's own lane; the commits before the lane's first marked loop-writer commit are exempt from this rung only (kitlib.provenance.loop_lane_window). Lane commits are read oldest first, each with its parents and tree, and each parent outside the range is read for its tree. The window opens at a loop claim or a marked loop-writer commit and closes at an attended re-claim with exactly one parent, a tree equal to that parent's, this branch's re-claim subject exactly, and no provenance trailer at all. A re-claim met while the window is closed changes nothing. The commits after a re-claim are exempt from this rung until the next marked loop-writer commit re-opens the window; a lane never marked has no window. The re-claim subject has one composer, which the coordinator's procedure and the reader use. commit_telemetry reports a refused telemetry commit instead of swallowing it.\"","+code_symbol = \"_claim_locked/_mint/commit_telemetry/_loop_trailer_refusal/_commit_object/LOOP_WRITER_SUBJECTS/loop_writer_commit/loop_lane_window/reclaim_subject/_reclaim/loop_claimed\"","+detail = \"The claim, refresh, merge, bookkeeping, handback-close and telemetry writers append format_loop_trailer to their messages; the claim and the mint do so through bookkeeping._commit_object, the commit helper both share. The commit-msg hook runs loop_trailer_refusal when the loop marker is set. integrate._loop_trailer_refusal, in the merge ladder, re-checks the commits of every loop lane whoever runs the slot, since plumbing commits and --no-verify commits never reach the hook and hooks are opt-in per checkout. A lane is the loop's when its claim, or any commit one of the loop's own writers made in its range, carries the trailer (kitlib.provenance.loop_writer_commit: a well-formed trailer and a subject a loop writer composes). Every commit of a loop lane must carry a present, well-formed trailer, a person's commit included, which otherwise belongs in the person's own lane; the commits before the lane's first marked loop-writer commit are exempt from this rung only (kitlib.provenance.loop_lane_window). Lane commits are read oldest first, each with its parents and tree, and each parent outside the range is read for its tree. The window opens at a loop claim or a marked loop-writer commit and closes at an attended re-claim with exactly one parent, a tree equal to that parent's, this branch's re-claim subject exactly, and no provenance trailer at all. A re-claim met while the window is closed changes nothing. The commits after a re-claim are exempt from this rung until the next marked loop-writer commit re-opens the window; a lane never marked has no window. The re-claim subject has one composer, which the coordinator's procedure and the reader use. commit_telemetry reports a refused telemetry commit instead of swallowing it. At the merge slot, a lane's claim record that cannot be read is refused, naming the read, and nothing is merged; it is never read as a lane the loop did not claim.\""," status = \"Approved\""," component = \"CMP-008\""," phase = 6"]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-946\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\test\\test-cases.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":2508,"oldLines":9,"newStart":2508,"newLines":9,"lines":[" [test.TC-242]"," verifies = [\"SR-209\", \"LLR-247\", \"LLR-248\", \"IF-194\", \"IF-197\"]"," level = \"Integration\"","-method = \"The trailer helpers unit-tested: format and parse round-trip, a session the grammar refuses cannot be formatted, the trailer joins the message's existing trailer block as git parses it, the last trailer wins, and a missing, malformed or other-session trailer is refused naming the subject, while with no session given any well-formed trailer passes. A child process started by the dispatcher and by the loop's main entry sees the marker, the session is told the trailer it owes, and that run's own commits name the same session; the launcher scripts never set it. Driven on real git repositories: with the marker set, the commit-msg hook refuses a commit with no trailer, naming its subject, and passes one with a valid trailer; without the marker a commit passes. The merge ladder refuses a loop lane whose range holds a plumbing commit without the trailer, merging nothing, and admits one whose every commit is marked; it judges a loop lane when the slot runs without the marker too; it judges no commit of a person's own lane, with or without the marker; and in a lane a person claimed and the loop later built, it exempts the commits before the first marked loop-writer commit and refuses a person's unmarked commit after it. The claim, refresh, merge, bookkeeping, handback-close, quarantine and telemetry writers each produce messages carrying the trailer, the refresh's attestation still verifies, the refresh, handback-close, quarantine, mechanical-close and telemetry messages each read as a loop writer's commit, and a refused telemetry commit is reported. Re-claim cases establish that: a lane claimed under the marker, re-claimed, then given an unmarked commit passes the trailer rung while the same commit before the re-claim is refused; a lane claimed attended and later marked by telemetry is judged from that mark and a later re-claim clears the window; a re-claim with a well-formed or malformed trailer, or another branch's subject, is not one; an exact-subject trailerless commit that changes the tree or has two parents neither closes the window nor escapes refusal by name; a marked loop-writer commit after a re-claim re-opens the window; a lane never marked stays a person's and the held-status rung judges a re-claimed lane whole; and a literal re-claim subject written by the earlier recipe reads the same as a composed one.\"","+method = \"The trailer helpers unit-tested: format and parse round-trip, a sess