r escapes refusal by name; a marked loop-writer commit after a re-claim re-opens the window; a lane never marked stays a person's and the held-status rung judges a re-claimed lane whole; and a literal re-claim subject written by the earlier recipe reads the same as a composed one. At the merge ladder, a loop lane whose claim record cannot be read is refused, naming the read, and nothing is merged.\""," tier = \"Full\"","-expected = \"Satisfies SR-209's acceptance: every loop-started process carries the marker; a loop commit without a valid trailer is refused naming its subject; a commit from a process the loop did not start passes where it is made, even while the loop runs; at the merge a lane is the loop's when its claim or a loop-writer commit in its range carries the trailer, every commit of a loop lane from its claim or its first marked loop-writer commit on must carry the trailer, a person's included, whoever runs the slot, and a person's own lane is not judged; the same rule wherever the floor runs. An attended re-claim recorded in the lane, a commit that changes nothing against its one parent, names that lane in the re-claim form, and carries no provenance trailer at all, ends the loop's window for the commits after it; a commit that fails any of those conditions is judged like any other; a later loop-writer commit re-opens the window.\"","+expected = \"Satisfies SR-209's acceptance: every loop-started process carries the marker; a loop commit without a valid trailer is refused naming its subject; a commit from a process the loop did not start passes where it is made, even while the loop runs; at the merge a lane is the loop's when its claim or a loop-writer commit in its range carries the trailer, every commit of a loop lane from its claim or its first marked loop-writer commit on must carry the trailer, a person's included, whoever runs the slot, and a person's own lane is not judged; the same rule wherever the floor runs. An attended re-claim recorded in the lane, a commit that changes nothing against its one parent, names that lane in the re-claim form, and carries no provenance trailer at all, ends the loop's window for the commits after it; a commit that fails any of those conditions is judged like any other; a later loop-writer commit re-opens the window. At the merge slot, a lane's claim record that cannot be read is refused, naming the read, and nothing is merged; it is never read as a lane the loop did not claim.\""," automated = \"Yes\""," evidence = \"tests/test_loop_provenance.py; tests/test_pre_commit_hook.py\""," status = \"Approved\""]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-946\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\README.md","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-946\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\acts.toml","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-946\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\requirements\\low-level-requirements.toml","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-946\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\test\\test-cases.toml"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01QUS17qSHHmNjhurgK6vzfu","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
